{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/780730-tools-of-the-trade","id":780730,"title":"Tools of the Trade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-05T15:09:58-08:00","id":780730,"title":"Tools of the Trade","content":"I've never played Hunter before, but getting involved in a game. I'm interested in playing an experienced Hunter that has just the right thing on hand for a given enemy without going crazy tech like Task Force VALKYRIE. More normal things like Silver Bullets, Dragons Breath Rounds for a Shotgun, maybe a Crossbow built to shoot wooden stacks at a Vampire, that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> So what kind of stuff would be useful to a Hunter? And probably just as importantly where can I find rules references to them? <br /> <br /> I figure this is probably a good topic of discussion to have floating around anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T18:27:14-08:00","id":780842,"title":"","content":"After watching Supernatural all my hunters always carry around a big thing of Morton's salt, great low-tech ghost countermeasure.<br /> <br /> Oh and it's listed on pg. 243 of the Rules Update","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Will Rotenberry</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer<br /> <b>Armory: Hurt Locker</b>","edited":{"userid":5031,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5031-bloodywillpower","user":"BloodyWillpower","date":".  Added page reference 12-05-2015, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5031-bloodywillpower","name":"BloodyWillpower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:05:00-08:00","id":780918,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I keep thinking salt, but I can't remember anything in WoD that Salt actually affects.<br /> A high tech digital video optic on a firearm would quickly ID a Vampire, shoot the blurry one. Don't know if there are stats for that one, haven't found it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:36:03-08:00","id":780938,"title":"","content":"Zip-ties, rope, tarp, stun gun, duct tape, container of gasoline, lighter fluid, lighter and matches, mace, mallet, bear trap, stake, rags and stick that can form a torch. Most of these are more for if there are people involved you might not necessarily want to kill, such as a person possessed by a ghost, a misguided cultist, a charmed servant and so forth. The video wouldn't necessarily help against vampires, they don't appear blurry in second edition. Do not underestimate mace, it slams targets with Stun and a nasty -5 penalty to all actions. Not so useful against zombies and ghosts but it can save you against a mage.<br /> <br /> Salt, when placed, forms a barrier to ghosts and demons that they cannot cross. When used in conjunction with a weapon, it allows one to damage and Discorporate ghosts. There are a few other items in the same book, the God Machine Chronicle. Flash paper, for example, can help identify vampires as when used it forces creatures vulnerable to fire to flinch, providing they fail a Resolve + Composure roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T06:18:41-08:00","id":781099,"title":"","content":"There are in fact two rules books that I would recommend for the kind of monster hunting equipment you are looking for. The first is the World of Darkness Armory. This gives you specs on all kinds of mundane equipment and how it operates in the nWoD. There is so much stuff in there that sometimes it's temping to say, &quot;Pfft! Mortals don't need powers! Look at this AGTM missile launcher my character picked up off of the black market!&quot; Still, even if the rules don't cover all of the weapons you're thinking of you can use some of the rules in there as a &quot;best fit&quot; for what you are trying to accomplish. Another rules book you might want to consult is the Slasher book for Hunter. In that book under tactics there are rules for making improvised weapons. Sometimes you need to pull a MacGuyver. Well the tactic of making an improvised weapon has that covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10065,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","user":"Zolace","date":". 12-06-2015, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T06:54:22-08:00","id":781115,"title":"","content":"A couple bottles of high proof alcohol (to go with the rags and lighter). Handy molotov cocktail against things vulnerable to fire, or a celebratory drink after a good raid (or liquid courage before a dangerous one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:41:41-08:00","id":781264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/780730-tools-of-the-trade?p=780918#post780918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I keep thinking salt, but I can't remember anything in WoD that Salt actually affects.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <b>GMC</b>, in section about Salt as equipment - it points that Salt works as universal Bane for ephemera of low Rank. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T13:23:18-08:00","id":781296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/780730-tools-of-the-trade?p=780938#post780938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Salt, when placed, forms a barrier to ghosts and demons that they cannot cross. When used in conjunction with a weapon, it allows one to damage and Discorporate ghosts. There are a few other items in the same book, the God Machine Chronicle. Flash paper, for example, can help identify vampires as when used it forces creatures vulnerable to fire to flinch, providing they fail a Resolve + Composure roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Salt is also used in folklore as defense against magic. Not actively used in nWoD but it's there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:10:24-08:00","id":781333,"title":"","content":"At least two cellphones, a smartphone for on the go research (nothing too deeply occult but anything you could learn at a public library should be available online) and a cheap burner phone for any legally questionable conversations you need to have over long distances (just ditch it before the cops show up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:01:29-08:00","id":781527,"title":"","content":"Or rather like 15 phones... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iW4ARc8jNgU\" data-code=\"iW4ARc8jNgU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iW4ARc8jNgU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}